   163→  it("allows free plan merchants to create up to 3 quizzes", async () => { /* ... */ });
   164→  it("blocks quiz creation at free plan limit with upgrade prompt", async () => { /* ... */ });
   165→  it("allows premium plan merchants unlimited quizzes", async () => { /* ... */ });
   166→  it("handles expired subscription gracefully", async () => { /* ... */ });
   167→  it("gates advanced features (conditional logic, integrations) to premium", async () => { /* ... */ });
   168→});
   169→```
   170→
   171→## 7. Public API and CORS Tests
   172→
   173→```typescript
   174→describe("public quiz API", () => {
   175→  it("returns CORS headers on OPTIONS request", async () => {
   176→    const request = new Request("http://localhost/api/public/quiz/abc123", { method: "OPTIONS" });
   177→    const response = await loader({ request, params: { id: "abc123" }, context: {} });
   178→    expect(response.headers.get("Access-Control-Allow-Origin")).toBeDefined();
   179→  });
   180→
   181→  it("returns published quiz data for valid quiz ID", async () => { /* ... */ });
   182→  it("returns 404 for draft quiz accessed via public API", async () => { /* ... */ });
   183→  it("validates quiz submission payload", async () => { /* ... */ });
   184→  it("rate limits excessive requests", async () => { /* ... */ });
   185→});
   186→```
   187→
   188→## 8. Quiz Flow End-to-End Tests
   189→
   190→```typescript
   191→describe("quiz taking flow", () => {
   192→  it("loads quiz with all questions in correct order", async () => { /* ... */ });
   193→  it("follows conditional branching based on answers", async () => { /* ... */ });
   194→  it("calculates correct product recommendations at end", async () => { /* ... */ });
   195→  it("saves response with all answers to database", async () => { /* ... */ });
   196→  it("handles quiz with no matching products gracefully", async () => { /* ... */ });
   197→  it("collects email when email capture is enabled", async () => { /* ... */ });
   198→});
   199→```
   200→
   201→# Test Patterns and Conventions
   202→
   203→**File naming:** `__tests__/[module].test.ts` or `__tests__/[component].test.tsx`
   204→**Test IDs:** Use `data-testid` attributes sparingly; prefer accessible queries (getByRole, getByLabelText)
   205→
   206→**Mock Patterns:**
   207→```typescript
   208→// Mock Shopify admin authentication
   209→const mockAuthenticate = {
   210→  admin: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({
   211→    session: { shop: "test-shop.myshopify.com", accessToken: "test-token" },
   212→    admin: {
   213→      graphql: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({
   214→        json: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ data: { products: { edges: [] } } }),
   215→      }),
   216→    },
   217→  }),
   218→  public: {
   219→    appProxy: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ session: null }),
   220→  },
   221→};
   222→```
   223→
   224→**Database Test Isolation:**
   225→- Use a test database (separate DATABASE_URL in .env.test)
   226→- Clean up test data in beforeEach/afterEach hooks
   227→- Use Prisma transactions for test isolation when possible
   228→- Never run tests against production database
   229→
   230→# Rules
   231→- Every new feature must include tests before it can be considered complete
   232→- Tests must be deterministic - no reliance on execution order or timing
   233→- No `test.skip` or `test.todo` in committed code (create issues instead)
   234→- Mock external services (Shopify API, email providers) - never call real APIs in tests
   235→- Test error paths as thoroughly as happy paths
   236→- Use descriptive test names that read as specifications
